{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — confirmed root cause (Phase 1 complete)\n\n**The detector is NOT broken. The test fixture has never been detectable.**\n\n### Mechanism\n\n`test_live_clone` writes two byte-identical 7-line JS files. That duplicated fragment is\n**32 tokens**. jscpd's default `--min-tokens` is **50**, so no clone fragment in the fixture\ncan ever reach the detection floor, and jscpd correctly reports `clones: 0`.\n\nEvidence (jscpd 5.0.14, `jscpd --debug` config dump on the exact fixture):\n\n    \"min_tokens\": 50,\n    \"min_lines\": 5,\n\nSame fixture, floor lowered:\n\n    jscpd --min-tokens 50 ./src -> {'clones': 0, 'sources': 0, 'tokens': 0}\n    jscpd --min-tokens 10 ./src -> {'clones': 1, 'sources': 2, 'tokens': 64,\n                                    'duplicatedTokens': 32, 'percentage': 42.86}\n\n### It is not a jscpd behaviour change\n\n`minTokens: 50` is the default in `@jscpd/core` **3.5.10**, **4.0.1**, and **5.x** (verified by\nunpacking each published tarball). The default has never differed, so no jscpd major-version\nchange can explain this.\n\n### It is not fixture drift or a detector regression\n\n`tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py` and\n`src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/_jscpd.py` were both introduced by a single commit,\n`dabf4c6ce2` (\"3ba0: add shared jscpd duplication analyzer\", 2026-07-23), and **neither file\nhas been modified since** (`git log --follow` returns exactly one commit for each).\n`--min-tokens` has never appeared anywhere in the source (`git log -S`).\n\n**Therefore the test was born RED.** It has never passed against a real jscpd on any version.\nCI skips it (jscpd is not installed there), so nothing ever observed the failure until a\ndeveloper with jscpd on PATH ran the suite.\n\n### AC3 — duplication is NOT silently zero (runtime proof through the real adapter)\n\n    rebar.metrics.analyzers.jscpd_dup.analyze(...) on jscpd 5.0.14:\n      ticket fixture (32 dup tokens)  -> {'clones': 0,   'percentage': 0.0}\n      same shape, >50 dup tokens      -> {'clones': 1,   'percentage': 48.81}\n      real tree src/rebar             -> {'clones': 194, 'percentage': 1.748}\n\nThe adapter's report parsing is fully compatible with jscpd 5.x and reports real clones on\nreal trees. The zero is specific to a sub-threshold fixture.\n\n### Disposition\n\nFix the fixture, not the assertion: enlarge the duplicated fragment comfortably past the\ndocumented 50-token floor so the test exercises the detection it claims to guard. The\nassertions `clones >= 1` / `percentage > 0` are unchanged. A negative control is added so a\nfuture genuine detector failure cannot pass vacuously."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786099874209391001,"uuid":"2feb654f-e512-44b5-ae92-2603380c4597"}